## Biographies
Dr. Zumin Wang graduated from University of Science Technology Beijing in 2018. After that he joined the Institute of Processing Engineering, Chinese Academy of Sciences, to work as a postdoc researcher under the supervision of Prof. Dan Wang. His research interests focused on the synthesis and applications of MOFsbased or MOFs-derived materials with hollow structures.
Prof. Nailiang Yang received his BS degree in Sun Yat-sen University, and then obtained his Doctor degree from University of Chinese Academy of Sciences in 2013 under the supervision of Professor Dan Wang. His thesis has been awarded as CAS Excellent Doctoral Dissertations. After graduation, he joined Professor Marie-Paule Pileni’s group as a postdoctoral fellow at Université Pierre et Marie Curie, France. Started from 2015, he worked as a Research Fellow in Professor Hua Zhang’s group at the School of Materials Science and Engineering in Nanyang Technological University (Singapore). Since 2018, he started working in the Institute of Process Engineering, CAS as a full professor. His research fields include the precise synthesis and assembly of nanomaterials, especially the 2D nanomaterials.
Prof. Dan Wang received his BS and MS at Jilin University (1994 and 1997) and Ph.D. at Yamanashi University (2001). He took his current position as a Principal Investigator at the Institute of Process Engineering, Chinese Academy of Sciences in 2004. His research interest is focused on the synthesis chemistry of multifunctional structure systems, including controllable synthesis of hollow multi-shelled structure, doping and complex of 2D materials and their applications for multi-component efficient electrode.
